        "original_id": "436d05d4-40cb-5104-96e6-972bfe8c7686",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Mickey Mouse Cup, North-West Derby\n- Organizations: Liverpool F.C., Manchester United F.C.\n- Topics: English football rivalries, football competitions\n\nFacts:\n- The term \"Mickey Mouse Cup\" is a subjective term in football, especially in English football, that is used negatively to describe a cup, league, or other competition as less important or less significant to a club or manager than other competitions.\n- Fans of Manchester United first coined the term \"Mickey Mouse Cup\" to disparage Liverpool's achievements and success in the League Cup.\n- The Liverpool F.C.–Manchester United F.C. rivalry is a high-profile inter-city rivalry between the English professional football clubs Liverpool and Manchester United.\n- The Liverpool F.C.–Manchester United F.C. rivalry is also known as the North-West Derby.\n- The Liverpool F.C.–Manchester United F.C. rivalry is considered one of the biggest rivalries in world football alongside the Old Firm derby, Superclásico, El Clásico, and Derby della Madonnina.\n- The Liverpool F.C.–Manchester United F.C. rivalry is considered the most famous fixture in English football.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
